abstract: >
  HERESY v3.0.0 is an offline browser artwork that serializes REST-like
  requests as fixed 80-column EBCDIC records. A bounded JCL parser approves
  the job, a COBOL DATA DIVISION defines the request layout, punched-card
  sequence columns order the deck, a FORTRAN computed GOTO chooses the
  response, and an Ada-derived policy governs fault recovery. Deterministic
  tests verify every transformation while CI limits the complete production
  build to 368,640 bytes, the capacity of one 360 KB 5.25-inch floppy disk.
